sty women  manages to bring back the whole cultured  crook versus crass con artist angle then  it's not difficult to guess who will  play her  overboard released in 1987 Gabi marshals  overboard may have divided critics but  it eventually won the hearts of comedy  fans around the world starring the  legendary couple of Kurt Russell and  Goldie Hawn the film focused on a  spoiled heiress who fell off a yacht and  woke up in a hospital with amnesia  through a series of hijinks her  carpenter tricked her into thinking she  was his wife and hillbilly hell broke  out well you you were crumpled I  flash-forward three decades and  overboard is being remade with Anna  Faris and a haenyeo debase in the lead  roles but this time there's a twist the  roles will be flipped with two BAE's  playing a selfish playboy from a wealthy  Mexican family who loses his memory  after taking a tumble off a boat while  Ferris will be a single mom who falls  Derby's into thinking he's her husband  when in doubts gender swap adults the  Thomas Crown Affair coming off films  like Creed and Fruitvale station  there's no denying Michael B Jordan is  one of the most exciting actors working  today now he'll be following in Steve  McQueen's footsteps with another  adaptation of the Thomas Crown Affair  the original 1968 film followed a  wealthy businessman who orchestrated a  nearly perfect bank robbery but  eventually an insurance investigator  began to suspect crown of pulling off  the heist sparks eventually flew between  them and the two leads had to grapple  with both their emotions and millions of  dollars as they try to outwit one  another the film was already remade with  some success with Pierce Brosnan and  Rene Russo as the co-leads  but what's really impressive is that  this new version is all Michael B  Jordans idea  Jordan reportedly pitched MGM on the  idea for a remake himself and landed the  title role as a result the raid  redemption one of the craziest action  movies in recent memory the raid  redemption followed a SWAT team trying  to nab a notorious crime lord but most  of the movie was made up of fantastic  fight scenes as the team battles away up  a heavily guarded high-rise apartment  building however while the original raid  is a martial arts extravaganza director  Joe Carnahan plans on getting grittier  with his upcoming remake the director of  films like narc and the gray car  is teaming up with actor Frank Grillo to  create a film he says will feel like a  feature-length version of the knife  fight scene in Saving Private Ryan  Deathwish the quintessential revenge  flick Michael winners death wish I saw a  pacifist turned killer declare war on  New York criminals after a gang of thugs  murdered his wife and raped his daughter  while the film stirred up quite a bit of  controversy back in the day death wish  was financially successful enough to  spawn several sequels what's the problem  now over 40 years later MGM has decided  to remake the dirty and gritty thriller  and possibly start a new series only  this time a Bruce Willis will be playing  the part of Paul Kersey  instead of Charles Bronson and Eli Roth  will step behind the camera for the  flick according to Roth we can expect to  see hostile style torture scenes with a  spectacular set pieces on this remake so  get ready to lose your appetite because  always comes true an American Werewolf  in London when it comes to werewolves  there's one film that stands snout and  shoulders above the rest an American  Werewolf in London is the quintessential  lycanthrope flick so universals upcoming  remake has some pretty big paw prints to  fill David Alpert and Robert Kirkman of  The Walking Dead Fame are set to produce  the new American werewolf bringing some  serious horror cred to the project  meanwhile Universal is keeping things in  the family on the filmmaking side hoping  to recapture the black magic of the  original the studio has brought out max  Landis  the son of the originals writer and  director John Landis to pen the  screenplay and helm the film so  hopefully this won't be just another bad  moon movie on the rise the great  outdoors one of John Hughes lesser-known  scripting efforts the great outdoors was  a 1988 comedy starring John candy as  Chet Ripley a Chicagoan who just wants  to spend some time with his family out  on the Wisconsin wilderness  unfortunately Chet's relaxing vacation  was ruined when his annoying  brother-in-law crashed the party with  his own family in tow leading to a  series of escapades involving water skis  a giant steak  and the bald-headed bear now Universal  Pictures is aiming to reboot the film  with Kevin Hart on board to lead whether  he plays chert or his brother-in-law  remains to be seen but we can count on  the funny man to deliver some memorable  moments and remind everyone what an  underrated gem the original was Scarface  say hello to a little remake of this  gangster classic as one of Al Pacino's  most acclaimed performances it's no  wonder fans are a bit skeptical about  anyone touching Brian De Palma's 1983  film but what most people don't know is  that Scarface was actually a remake  itself the first Scarface was filmed in  1932 and it featured an Italian  immigrant making a name for himself in  the Chicago mob a couple of decades  later the Pomo simply switched the  setting to Miami turns the main  character into a Cuban and created an  all-time masterpiece in keeping with the  Scarface we make tradition the new film  will take place in Los Angeles and  follow a Mexican immigrants rise to  power Diego Luna will play the main  character working with a screenplay  written by boardwalk Empire's Terence  winter and doctored by the Coen brothers  you might recall that the last time the  sibling duo had anything to do with a  script about drugs murder and Mexican  cartels it worked out pretty well so  maybe we should be optimistic about  Scarface as modern-day revival the  intouchables when the intouchables made  its way to America in 2012 the film was  not a commercial success but overseas  this French drama made an absolute  killing the story focused on the  relationship between a paralyzed man  named Philippe and his Senegalese  caretaker dress in addition to race the  two are separated by class and the  different world views but over the  course of the film  the two form a bond and help each other  become better people now The Weinstein  Company is giving Americans another  chance to see the movie only this time  they'll get to hear all the dialogue in  English retitled untouchable the  upcoming remake will star Bryan Cranston  as a wheelchair-bound Philip and Kevin  Hart will play Dell Phillips new  assistant from the Bronx Nicole Kidman  will also star and Neil Berger will  direct the pick or bow in two theaters  and March 2018 Starship Troopers  directed by Paul Verhoeven  starship troopers has never gotten the  same amount of love as the door  des magnum opus Robocop but it still  gained a sizable cult following over the  years the 1997 original followed a group  of kids who joined the military to fight  the bugs in outer space  initially the movie was misunderstood by  quite a few critics but these days  troopers has widely recognized as a  biting satire on fascism the original  novel written by Robert a Heinlein  couldn't be more different the book has  a much more Pro War stance than of a  joven film which means the upcoming  remake or diverge significantly Columbia  Pictures hopes to kick off a potential  franchise with a new Starship Troopers  but most importantly the upcoming  version will stick a lot closer to the  novel maniac cop directed by the  infamous William Lustig 1988 maniac cop  has been described as lucky and scummy  and actually kind of fun the  exploitation flick features Tom Atkins  as a cop investigating a series of  murders  Robert Sedaris a psychopathic police  officer killing anyone in his path and  the Bruce Campbell as an innocent cop  caught in the middle while the film  wasn't exactly a critical hits the  slasher had picked up a cult following  over the years the maniac cop remake has  been in the works since 2012 but in 2015  things really started moving Marvel and  DC Comics writer edy frou Baker is  writing the script with John Hyams  directing in March 2017 Variety reported  that the film would start shooting in  the summer  although the remake isn't going to be  exactly the same as the stig's original  B picture this time Maniac Cop will be  more of a realistic thriller than a  horror film with producer Nicolas  Winding raffinate Elling a Bloody  Disgusting the new film will serve as  more of a commentary on modern day  society and the sometimes questionable  actions of law enforcement there's no  word yet on who's starring but whoever  they pick they all probably pale in  comparison to Cumberlands Adar at least  when it comes to their chins anyway  thanks for watching click the loop icon  to subscribe to our YouTube channel plus  check out all this cool stuff we know  your love to  [Applause]

